WEBVTT

00:00:07.216 --> 00:00:16.034
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> You are juggling some five balls in the air: work, family, health, friends, and spirit.

00:00:16.589 --> 00:00:21.658
Work is a rubber ball. If you drop it, it will bounce back.

00:00:22.849 --> 00:00:29.675
But the other four balls are made of glass. If you drop one of these, they will never be the same.

00:00:30.922 --> 00:00:34.069
You must understand that and strive for balance in your life.

00:00:37.183 --> 00:00:41.140
It can sometimes seem as if life is just one long list of things to do.

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:46.311
There are the demands of a stressful job, dealing with constant meetings,

00:00:46.661 --> 00:00:52.152
deadlines, emails, and phone calls.

00:00:54.653 --> 00:00:58.396
And then there’s the housework, shopping, childcare,

00:00:58.396 --> 00:01:03.386
and cooking to fit in before we can even think about finding time to see friends,

00:01:03.862 --> 00:01:06.700
chat with the family, and chill out.

00:01:09.247 --> 00:01:13.888
No wonder so many people find it difficult to get their work–life balance right.

00:01:15.356 --> 00:01:21.215
But creating that balance and making the space in our busy lives is central to our happiness and well-being.

00:01:24.771 --> 00:01:28.556
There’s plenty of research to show that many of us struggle to achieve

00:01:28.556 --> 00:01:31.604
the right balance between work and the rest of our life,

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:36.642
between the things we must or should do and the things we’d like to do.

00:01:38.451 --> 00:01:42.338
As a result, we frequently feel overstressed and under-rested.

00:01:44.332 --> 00:01:51.498
In the UK, a typical employee works for around 38 hours per week and takes 28 days’ holiday a year.

00:01:54.202 --> 00:01:57.991
Sixty per cent of employees say they work longer hours than they would like,

00:01:59.039 --> 00:02:03.410
with 20% saying they often or always feel exhausted in their work.

00:02:06.064 --> 00:02:10.949
Office workers, for example, say they are frequently expected to work in their spare time,

00:02:11.084 --> 00:02:13.896
replying to emails or taking out-of-hours calls.

00:02:14.436 --> 00:02:20.610
In fact, research suggests people work an extra eight unpaid hours each week this way.

00:02:25.363 --> 00:02:29.038
And for many, this work culture is unsustainable.

00:02:30.614 --> 00:02:35.596
Two thirds of UK workers say they have suffered a work-related health issue in the last year,

00:02:35.754 --> 00:02:39.462
with two of the most common being anxiety and disrupted sleep patterns.

00:02:42.737 --> 00:02:46.893
More than a quarter said their job had a negative impact on their personal life.

00:02:49.357 --> 00:02:51.588
And this is a problem for employers, too.

00:02:52.524 --> 00:02:59.531
In the UK, employee burnout costs British businesses around £45 billion per year.